      <TextArea editable="false" layoutX="63.0" layoutY="135.0" prefHeight="769.0" prefWidth="926.0" text="Turn Sequence&#10;Each turn follows a strict sequence representing one complete action on the Floor:&#10;1. Powerup Phase (Optional):&#10;○ Current player may choose to activate their powerup if they have enough energy (500 energy cost)&#10;2. Dice Roll:&#10;○ Roll a standard 6-sided dice (1-6)&#10;○ The number rolled indicates the number of cells the player will move forward&#10;3. Movement Attempt:&#10;○ Player attempts to move to the new cell based on dice roll&#10;○ Occupied Cell Check: If the final destination cell (after card/transport cells) is occupied by the opponent, the move is invalid&#10;■ Player remains at their current position&#10;■ Player must roll again (retry the turn)&#10;4. Cell Action:&#10;○ If the move is valid (cell not occupied), the player lands on the new cell&#10;○ The landed cell's special effect activates&#10;○ Cell effects may modify position, energy, or other game states&#10;5. Board Update:&#10;○ Board is updated with the new monster positions&#10;○ All game state changes are finalized&#10;6. Turn Switch:&#10;○ If the win condition is not met, turn passes to the other player&#10;○ If the win condition is met, the game ends&#10;&#10;Win Condition&#10;● A player wins when ALL of the following are true:&#10;○ Player's position is exactly at cell 99 (Boo's Door - the final cell)&#10;○ Player has ≥ 1000 energy in their canister&#10;● If win condition is not met:&#10;○ The game continues with the next player's turn&#10;○ Players loop through turns until someone achieves both victory requirements" wrapText="true">
